issues=[
('High','Condition coverage remains incomplete','Seven original topic IDs receive structured regimens; the other 149 do not. Of 28 manually flagged treatment/prophylaxis/stewardship entries, 21 have no linked antibiotic lesson. This is a count of entries, not unique diseases or an exam-weighting estimate.'),
('High','Retained historical teaching needs reconciliation','Priority examples: necrotizing-infection empiric coverage; legacy UTI duration/classification; AOM allergy/failure branches; cirrhosis/SBP diagnosis; Lyme age restrictions. Existing limitation text warns about several of these, but a warning is not a correction. Newly read sources corroborate the SSTI, cUTI and Lyme scope issues; the SBP error is also documented in the repository backlog and requires source-specific remediation.'),
('High','Organ evidence remains incomplete','All 18 named drugs in antibiotic-tagged lessons have selective safety profiles. Four profiles have renal status not_established: penicillin V, azithromycin, fosfomycin and benzathine penicillin G. Seven have hepatic status not_established: amoxicillin, penicillin V, fosfomycin, levofloxacin, fidaxomicin, oral vancomycin and benzathine penicillin G. This is an evidence gap in the loaded extract, not proof that a dose reduction is medically required or that none is needed.'),
('High','Population and route limits are material','Pediatric, pregnancy/breastfeeding, dialysis and hepatic-severity teaching remains selective. Strep pediatric dosing does not establish pediatric organ tables. Oral vancomycin CDI evidence cannot support IV vancomycin for sepsis, pneumonia or endocarditis. Some label/guideline differences are already disclosed, including nitrofurantoin kidney thresholds and CAP durations; preserve and resolve their scopes.'),
('Medium','Supplemental condition integration is incomplete','No supplemental condition has a linked antibiotic regimen. Otitis externa explicitly lacks exact drops/dosing; endocarditis and rheumatic fever are diagnostic-only. Static code inspection shows ordinary guided topics call regimenInstructions(), while supplemental condition specialist instructions load criteria but not linked regimen instructions. Adding data mappings alone would not wire antibiotic teaching into those specialist condition lessons.'),
('Medium','The existing audit does not measure the promised outcome','audit.mts inventories names, sources, profiles and lessons; it does not produce a per-condition completeness matrix. foundInRegimenLessons searches the JSON of all base lessons, so a safety/advanced-text mention can count as found. coverage.ts gives every unlinked topic complete_regimen_not_verified, including unrelated topics, and its SBP regex also matches systolic blood pressure.'),
('Medium','Metadata is stale and counts can mislead','curriculum.json still says medication safety covers 11 named drugs across 13 existing regimen lessons, although actual totals are 23 safety profiles and 34 medication lessons. The 27 antibiotic-tagged lessons include antiprotozoal trichomoniasis/giardiasis uses; the 18-drug figure counts distinct named entities including a combination drug. Giardia has no topic_ids mapping and is standalone only. None of these counts proves breadth by condition.'),
('Release gate','Do not mark expansion complete','No condition is demonstrated complete against the full agreed all-applicable-scenarios standard. This does not mean the stored regimens are all wrong: it means partial data, unresolved evidence and independent review limits prevent a completeness claim. No app data, main branch, deployment or assessment bank was changed by this audit.'),
]
acceptance=[
'Every original and supplemental entry has an explicit relevance decision; every applicable syndrome is broken into population, severity, route, treatment versus prophylaxis, and supported alternative/escalation branches. A guideline need not define a universal first/second/third-line ladder.',
'Each included branch has drug/formulation, units, route, interval and duration; weight-based doses state mg/kg/day versus mg/kg/dose and caps where supported. Maximum not applicable, not established and missing must remain distinct.',
'Contraindication, avoid-use, precaution/monitoring and no-adjustment claims are differentiated and sourced. Organ guidance specifies the measure, threshold, baseline regimen, formulation and population. Dialysis and combined organ dysfunction are separately addressed or explicitly outside scope.',
'Disease guidance supports selection and course; product-specific evidence supports medication safety. Record the exact URL, section and source/access dates. A registered link or a retrieved page is not a checked stored lesson.',
'Reconcile known old/new conflicts in the loaded topic text. Test both ordinary topic and supplemental specialist navigation to ensure the correct regimen and component profiles reach the tutor.',
'Add meaningful data and behavior checks for missing branches, aliases, combination components, route/population mismatches and evidence linkage; keep assessment isolation and progress behavior. Independent clinical/pharmacy review and real generated-teaching checks remain distinct from software tests.',
'Release reporting must list complete, partial, excluded and pending scenarios with reasons and verified deployed identity. Completion requires closing or explicitly agreeing the remaining scope gaps, not reaching an arbitrary drug/lesson count.',
]
plan=[
('1','Correct known problematic retained antibiotic claims','SSTI/necrotizing infection, AOM, UTI/cUTI, cirrhosis/SBP and Lyme; preserve useful content while replacing unsupported statements with exact scoped evidence.'),
('2','Close common outpatient lesson gaps','Otitis media, bacterial sinusitis, cellulitis/abscess and otitis externa; complete strep allergy branches and reconcile duplicates.'),
('3','Complete the partly covered condition families','Pyelonephritis/cUTI and pregnancy branches; inpatient/severe CAP; STI complication/allergy pathways; CDI fulminant/recurrence branches.'),
('4','Complete remaining indicated or prophylactic uses','H. pylori, Lyme, selected COPD exacerbations, acne/secondary skin infection, cirrhosis/HE, HIV OI pathways, prenatal prophylaxis, sickle-cell pathways, pleural/pancreatic/perianal infection, sepsis, endocarditis and rheumatic fever. Maintain source-control and specialist scope.'),
('5','Wire and verify the full condition matrix','Ensure ordinary and supplemental condition lessons load the right evidence, correct stale metadata/count semantics, and publish a reviewable coverage result before calling the expansion complete.'),
]
report=dict(audit_date='2026-10-17',baseline_commit=BASE_COMMIT,branch='feature/medication-safety-advanced-2026-10-17',live_health=dict(url='https://fm-socratic-voice-tutor-private-test.up.railway.app/api/healthz',observed_status='ok',curriculum_version='antibiotic-regimens-2026-10-17-v4',library_version='refresh-2026-10-15-ae430fbadf7a',limitation='Live health matches local version and counts; endpoint does not expose deployed commit. No authenticated live catalog or voice-output check performed in this audit.'),stats=stats,method='All 156 original topic titles and stored content screened; original snapshot independently reproduced from runtime seed/corrections/evidence/backlog and matched byte-for-byte after JSON serialization. All 12 supplemental condition lessons and all 27 antibiotic-tagged regimens inspected. Manual scope judgments are explicit in this generator. Source registry/profile integrity checked; selected official guidance newly read for corroboration. Product labels and every clinical claim were not independently revalidated.',original_topics=rows,supplemental_conditions=extras,regimens=regimens,issues=[dict(priority=p,title=t,finding=f) for p,t,f in issues],newly_read_sources=external,acceptance=acceptance,implementation_sequence=plan,original_source_sha256={p:hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in ['docs/guideline-refresh/candidate-library.json','artifacts/api-server/voice-tutor/curriculum.json','artifacts/api-server/voice-tutor/expanded-curriculum.json','artifacts/api-server/voice-tutor/core.ts','artifacts/api-server/voice-tutor/coverage.ts']})
(HERE/'audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')

esc=lambda v:html.escape(str(v),quote=True)
def link(url,label=None):
    return f'<a href="{esc(url)}">{esc(label or url)}</a>' if url else 'None'
def table(headers,rr):
    return '<div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(h)+'</th>' for h in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+cell+'</td>' for cell in row)+'</tr>' for row in rr)+'</tbody></table></div>'

sections=[]
sections.append('<p class="eyebrow">FM COPILOT · CONTENT COVERAGE AUDIT · 17 OCTOBER 2026</p><h1>The antibiotic expansion is still partial.</h1><p class="lead">Only <b>7 of 156 original library entries</b> have linked antibiotic regimen lessons. The current build does not demonstrate the agreed condition-by-condition completeness.</p>')
sections.append('<div class="metrics">'+''.join(f'<div><b>{n}</b><span>{esc(label)}</span></div>' for n,label in [(156,'original entries screened'),(12,'supplemental conditions'),(27,'antibiotic-tagged lessons'),(18,'named drugs'),(28,'entries needing treatment / prophylaxis / stewardship review'),(21,'of those entries have no linked lessons')])+'</div>')
sections.append('<p><b>Verdict:</b> 7 original entries have partial linked coverage; 21 other flagged original entries have no linked lesson. Four supplemental entries need treatment/prophylaxis scope or conditional linkage review. These are entry counts, with duplicate condition families retained, not counts of unique diseases. No condition has been demonstrated complete under the full agreed standard.</p><p><b>Live check:</b> Health reports <code>antibiotic-regimens-2026-10-17-v4</code>, 156 library topics, 116 specialist lessons, 23 safety profiles and 490 inventory entities. Local library digest matches the live digest. Health does not expose a deployed commit, so exact live source identity is not independently proven here.</p>')
sections.append('<nav>'+''.join(f'<a href="#{a}">{b}</a>' for a,b in [('findings','Findings'),('priority','Priority gaps'),('ledger','All 156 entries'),('supplemental','12 supplements'),('regimens','27 regimens'),('sources','Sources'),('completion','Completion standard')])+'</nav>')
sections.append('<h2 id="findings">What the audit found</h2>'+''.join(f'<article><span class="tag">{esc(p)}</span><h3>{esc(t)}</h3><p>{esc(f)}</p></article>' for p,t,f in issues))
sections.append('<h2 id="priority">Condition families requiring work</h2><p>The following is a gap ledger, not a prescribing protocol. “No linked lesson” can coexist with useful doses or checked claims in the original topic. Those fragments have not been treated as complete regimens.</p>'+table(['Family / current entry','Linked lessons','Required completion'],[[esc(rows[i]['group'])+'<br><small>'+esc(rows[i]['title'])+'</small>',str(len(rows[i]['linked_lesson_ids'])),esc(rows[i]['gap'])] for i in scope]))
sections.append('<h2 id="ledger">All 156 original library entries</h2><p>Every entry is retained, including duplicates. Treatment relevance is a manual audit judgment based on the stored scope. “No direct scope identified” does not mean antibiotics could never be appropriate for a separately diagnosed complication.</p><label>Filter audit tables <input id="filter" type="search" placeholder="Condition, topic ID, drug, gap…"></label><p id="filterStatus" aria-live="polite"></p>'+table(['Index / topic ID','Stored topic','Audit classification','Linked regimen IDs','Evidence / remaining work'],[[str(r['index'])+'<br><code>'+esc(r['topic_id'])+'</code>',esc(r['title']),esc(r['relevance'])+'<br><b>'+esc(r['status'])+'</b>',('<br>'.join(esc(x) for x in r['linked_lesson_ids']) or 'None'),esc(r['gap'])+'<details><summary>Stored source/review metadata</summary><p>Stored review: '+esc(r['stored_review'])+'</p>'+(''.join('<p>'+link(e['url'],e['id'])+' · '+esc(e['locator'])+'</p>' for e in r['stored_evidence']) or '<p>No individually tagged evidence records.</p>')+'<p>Legacy citation: '+link(r['legacy_source_url'])+'</p><p>A link alone does not verify a complete antibiotic lesson.</p></details>'] for r in rows]))
sections.append('<h2 id="supplemental">All 12 supplemental condition lessons</h2><p>None has a linked structured antibiotic regimen. Diagnostic-only entries remain available, with their limited scope stated.</p>'+table(['Lesson','Classification','Gap'],[[esc(r['title'])+'<br><code>'+esc(r['topic_id'])+'</code>',esc(r['classification']),esc(r['gap'])+'<details><summary>Stored limitations</summary>'+''.join('<p>'+esc(g)+'</p>' for g in r['stored_lesson_gaps'])+'</details>'] for r in extras]))
sections.append('<h2 id="regimens">All 27 stored antibiotic-tagged regimens</h2><p>All nine regimen fields are populated in each lesson; every explicitly named component has a safety profile, and every source ID resolves. Those structural checks do not establish clinical completeness or independent accuracy. “Not established” describes the loaded evidence, not permission to use an unadjusted dose. Giardia is a standalone antiprotozoal lesson and has no condition mapping.</p>'+table(['Lesson / links','Kidney evidence status','Liver evidence status','Stored gaps / sources'],[[esc(r['title'])+'<br><code>'+esc(r['id'])+'</code><br>'+('Mapped to '+str(len(r['topic_ids']))+' original entry IDs' if r['topic_ids'] else '<b>No topic mapping</b>'),'<br>'.join(esc(p['drug']+': '+p['status']) for p in r['renal_evidence']),'<br>'.join(esc(p['drug']+': '+p['status']) for p in r['hepatic_evidence']),''.join('<p>'+esc(g)+'</p>' for g in r['gaps'])+'<details><summary>Registered sources and scoped organ guidance</summary>'+''.join('<p>'+link(sources[s]['url'],s)+' · '+esc(sources[s].get('sections',''))+'</p>' for s in r['source_ids'])+''.join('<p><b>'+esc(p['drug'])+' kidney:</b> '+esc(p['guidance'])+'</p>' for p in r['renal_evidence'])+''.join('<p><b>'+esc(p['drug'])+' liver:</b> '+esc(p['guidance'])+'</p>' for p in r['hepatic_evidence'])+'</details>'] for r in regimens]))
sections.append('<h2 id="sources">Evidence inspected and audit limits</h2><p>'+esc(report['method'])+'</p><p>Newly retrieved sources below corroborate selected coverage requirements and conflicts. They have not been ingested into the app or promoted into stored checked regimen lessons by this audit. Existing source records and selectively checked topic facts remain separate from these newly read pages. Comprehensive freshness surveillance and independent clinician/pharmacist review remain pending.</p>'+table(['Newly read official source','Audit finding'],[[link(s['url'],s['title']),esc(s['finding'])] for s in external]))
sections.append('<h2 id="completion">What must be true before calling the expansion complete</h2><ol>'+''.join('<li>'+esc(a)+'</li>' for a in acceptance)+'</ol><h3>Recommended implementation order</h3>'+table(['Order','Work','Scope'],[[esc(a),esc(b),esc(c)] for a,b,c in plan]))
sections.append('<h2>Traceability</h2><p>Repository baseline: '+link('https://github.com/aibotjock/fm-resident-copilot/commit/'+BASE_COMMIT,BASE_COMMIT[:12])+' on <code>feature/medication-safety-advanced-2026-10-17</code>. Audit work is isolated on <code>audit/antibiotic-condition-coverage-2026-10-17</code>. No implementation or deployment change is part of this report.</p><details><summary>Reproducibility and source digests</summary><p>Reproduce with <code>python3 docs/voice-tutor/antibiotic-audit-2026-10-17/build_report.py</code>. The JSON ledger and generator accompany this HTML in the repository working branch. All-topic runtime/snapshot comparison, count assertions, source resolution and profile attachment checks passed.</p><pre>'+esc(json.dumps(report['original_source_sha256'],indent=2))+'</pre></details><p class="foot">Educational software content audit. This report documents coverage and evidence limitations; it does not provide a clinically validated prescribing formulary.</p>')
css='''body{margin:0;background:#f3f5f7;color:#172735;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1250px;margin:auto;padding:38px 26px 70px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,54px);line-height:1.12;max-width:920px}h2{margin-top:54px;border-top:2px solid #cbd7dd;padding-top:24px}h3{margin:8px 0}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#35646f}.lead{font-size:21px;max-width:1000px}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px;margin:28px 0}.metrics div{background:white;border:1px solid #d5e0e5;padding:18px;border-radius:10px}.metrics b{display:block;font-size:34px;color:#006b70}.metrics span{display:block;font-size:14px}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:15px;background:#e4edf0;padding:16px;border-radius:8px}a{color:#005d74}article{background:white;border-left:4px solid #ad7140;padding:18px 22px;margin:14px 0;border-radius:6px}.tag{font-size:12px;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:750;color:#8b5427}.tablewrap{overflow:auto;margin:20px 0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:white;font-size:14px}th{text-align:left;background:#163b47;color:white;padding:12px;position:sticky;top:0}td{padding:13px;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #dae2e7;min-width:130px}td:last-child{min-width:300px}td p{margin:0 0 10px}code{font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}small{color:#4d626e}input{font:inherit;width:min(90%,600px);display:block;padding:12px;border:1px solid #9bb0b9;border-radius:6px;background:white}label{font-weight:650}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#255f71;font-weight:600}details{margin-top:10px}pre{overflow:auto;font-size:12px}.foot{font-size:13px;color:#506773;margin-top:40px}li{margin:12px 0}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:24px 15px}.metrics{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}td{min-width:150px}}@media print{body{background:white;font-size:11px}main{max-width:none;padding:0}nav,label,#filterStatus{display:none}h1{font-size:28px}h2{break-after:avoid}th{position:static}td{font-size:10px;min-width:0!important}a{color:inherit}article{break-inside:avoid}.tablewrap{overflow:visible}code{font-size:9px}}'''
script='''document.getElementById('filter').addEventListener('input',e=>{let n=0;const q=e.target.value.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll('tbody tr').forEach(r=>{r.hidden=!r.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q);if(!r.hidden)n++});document.getElementById('filterStatus').textContent=q?n+' matching rows across all audit tables':'';});'''
(HERE/'FM_Copilot_Antibiotic_Coverage_Audit_2026-10-17.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>FM Copilot — Antibiotic Coverage Audit</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main>'+''.join(sections)+'</main><script>'+script+'</script></body></html>')
